[version]
1.7.0
[date]
2026-10-22
[whatsnew]
- FIXED: Bootloader menu now shows correctly!
  - Completely rewritten showMenu() with proper cursor positioning
  - Items displayed with number prefix (1. archos, 2. craftos)
  - Selected item highlighted with inverted colors
  - Arrow keys + Enter OR number keys to select
  - No more rendering glitches (old code mixed setCursorPos and write)
- FIXED: CraftOS boot "loop in gettable" error!
  - Old: tried to run vanilla shell via os.run(_G, shellPath) inside
    ArchOS-CC's polluted _G → require() crashed
  - New: craftos-shim moves /startup.lua to /startup.lua.bak and reboots
    CC:T boots with NO startup.lua → pure vanilla shell with clean _G
  - On next boot: startup.lua detects /tmp/restore-startup marker,
    restores startup.lua.bak → /startup.lua, reboots back to ArchOS-CC
- NEW: Installer self-update!
  - Installer checks repo for newer version of installer.lua
  - Extracts INSTALLER_VERSION constant from both local and remote
  - If remote is newer: asks user, downloads, replaces, re-runs
  - Ensures users always have the latest installer
- NEW: Installer only downloads files from MANIFEST
  - Does NOT download entire repo contents
  - MANIFEST is a curated list of required files
  - If repo has extra folders (programs/, etc.) they're NOT downloaded
  - Users can create separate repos for extra programs
- FIXED: Mouse Y coordinate (from v1.6.6)
  - Was off by 1 (extra -1 in resumeMouse)
  - All mouse clicks in windowed apps now land correctly
[/whatsnew]
[files]
bootloader/bootloader.lua
startup.lua
kernel/craftos-shim.lua
installer.lua
de/gui.lua
latest_update.upd
[/files]
